# Jira register (live-read 2026-08-21)

- Cloud: `https://eliteintegrityservices.atlassian.net` — project **P2024** (Elite Integrity - Engineering)
- REST v3 with operator email + API token. **Never store tokens in this folder.**
- Types: **Project** (job) → **Task** (package) → **Sub-task** (drawing). Dummy job `P2024-15553` spawned this template.

## One drawing = Sub-task under Drawing Package

- Label `Drafting`. Parent task e.g. `2026-Tanzim Drawing Package`. Job Project is the grandparent.
- Dummy drawings: `P2024-15578` `2026-Tanzim-1-1 Drawing-1`, `P2024-15579` `2026-Tanzim-1-2 Drawing-2`
- Live summary shape: `2026-075-1-STWD SPIRAL STAIRWAY: INSIDE HANDRAIL DETAIL` — first token = drawing ID; rest = title. Job Number field is the grouping key.

## Field map

| Use | Field | ID |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Job | Job Number | `customfield_10300` |
| Outgoing revision (what we send) | Outgoing Rev | `customfield_10280` (A–E, 0–15, 0A/1A/2A, N/A) |
| Purpose | Submitted to Client For | `customfield_10281` (Approval / Info / Planned / NA) |
| Incoming rev | Incoming Rev | `customfield_10283` |
| Client stamp | Client Approval Status | `customfield_10284` |
| Shop / Field IFC rev | Shop IFC Rev / Field IFC Rev | `customfield_10285` / `customfield_10287` |
| Client dwg no. | Client Document Number | `customfield_10279` (text; editable on the DocCon pack, Confirm writes it) |
| Drawing class | EDDI Status | `customfield_10289` (drawings: `1 - Fabrication Drawings - EDDI`) |

Sub-task statuses: To Do, In Progress, OFA, Awaiting Client Information, Roadblock, Back from Client, IFI, IFC, Done.

Template also has Task `Document Transmittals` (label `DocCon`) — a work package, not the drawing register.

Log numbering (locked 2026-09-01): `CT|ST|FT-{Job Number}-{n}` from the job Excel books under `3.0 Doc Con`. Client STATUS list: APPROVAL, CONSTRUCTION, INFORMATION, REVIEW, AS-BUILT (not the same labels as Jira purpose).

Controllers today edit those fields in a Jira Excel export. That file is not a second register. They will edit the same fields **on the DocCon console**; confirm writes Jira REST on the drawing sub-task.

